hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19171","Ali ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Jabir ibn Subh narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Khuzai narrated to me, and I accompanied him to Wasit, and he named Allah at the first of his food and at the last morsel, saying: In the name of Allah in its first and last. So I said to him: You name at the first of what you eat; what of your saying at the last of what you eat: In the name of Allah its first and last? He said: I tell you of that: my grandfather Umayya ibn Makhshi, of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I heard him say: A man ate while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) watched, and he did not name until at the last of his food a morsel, when he said: In the name of Allah its first and last. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan kept eating with him until he named, then nothing remained in his belly but he vomited it."
